PlatformBmPrintScLib: print only boot failures, not every load/start

BdsDxe printed "BdsDxe: loading Boot0001 ..." and "starting ..." to the
console for every boot, over the boot logo (and above the Windows boot
spinner, which keeps the firmware screen). Keep the failure reports only.

--- a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformBmPrintScLib/StatusCodeHandler.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformBmPrintScLib/StatusCodeHandler.c
@@ -93,12 +93,11 @@
   CHAR16                        *DevPathString;
 
   //
-  // Ignore all status codes that are irrelevant for LoadImage() and
-  // StartImage() preparations and return codes.
+  // Ignore all status codes other than LoadImage() and StartImage() failures.
+  // The "loading" / "starting" lines for every boot would be drawn over the
+  // boot logo; a failed boot option is still reported.
   //
-  if ((Value != mLoadPrep) && (Value != mLoadFail) &&
-      (Value != mStartPrep) && (Value != mStartFail))
-  {
+  if ((Value != mLoadFail) && (Value != mStartFail)) {
     return EFI_SUCCESS;
   }
 
